  "content": {
    "title": "Mexico vs. Portugal: Time, date, TV channel and how to watch today",
    "text": "March 28, 2026, 1:00 p.m. ETMexico and Portugal meet Saturday at Estadio Banorte (formerly Azteca) in Mexico City in an international friendly that doubles as a test event for the iconic stadium ahead of the 2026 FIFA World Cup this summer.The match marks the grand re-opening of the stadium, which has been closed for two years as it's undergone renovations ahead of the World Cup.El Tri enter this summer with the weight of being a co-host nation on their backs and the pressure of finally getting past the round of 16 in front of their home supporters.Mexico will bring a depleted roster into the March window, with fixtures like captain Edson Álvarez, Luis Malagón, Marcel Ruiz, César Huerta, Santiago Giménez, Gilberto Mora and more all out injured.Watch Mexico vs. Portugal on FuboPortugal arrives as a strong candidate to lift the trophy at the end of the summer. However, captain Cristiano Ronaldo has been ruled out after suffering a hamstring injury. He is joined on the absentee list by Rúben Dias, Bernardo Silva, and Nélson Semedo.Roberto Martínez still has plenty of quality to work with, as Bruno Fernandes leads a midfield featuring Vitinha, João Neves, and debutant Mateus Fernandes, while Gonçalo Ramos, Pedro Neto, Rafael Leão, and João Félix give A Seleção enough attacking firepower to test Mexico's defense.Portugal will face the United States on Tuesday in the second match of the March window, while Mexico faces Belgium.Mexico vs. Portugal prediction, pickPortugal is the better side on paper even without Ronaldo, Dias, and Bernardo Silva, but a sold-out Azteca at altitude is one of the toughest environments in world soccer. Mexico's Gold Cup form and home-field advantage make this a competitive match, but Portugal's midfield depth should be enough to get a result.Prediction: Mexico 1, Portugal 2Mexico vs. Portugal channel, start time, streamingWhen: Saturday, March 28Where: Estadio Azteca (Mexico City, Mexico)Time: 9 p.m. ETChannel/streaming: Fox Deportes (Watch on Fubo), ViX (Watch on Prime Video), Univision, TUDN",
